{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"178\t/**\n179\t * How far a transcript has been captured: the line count consumed, and the\n180\t * file size that line count corresponded to.\n181\t *\n182\t * `size` exists for the catch-up sweep (see `sweepStaleTranscripts`), which\n183\t * needs to answer \"did this file grow since we last read it\" for every\n184\t * session in a project without reading them all. A cursor written by an\n185\t * older cledger has no `size`; that reads as 0, so the file looks grown and\n186\t * gets re-read once, which dedups.\n187\t */\n188\tinterface Cursor {\n189\t  lines: number;\n190\t  size: number;\n191\t}\n192\t\n193\t/**\n194\t * The cursor recorded for a session, or null when there is none.\n195\t *\n196\t * The null is load-bearing, and is not the same as `{lines: 0}`: \"cledger has\n197\t * never captured this session\" is what gates the sweep (see\n198\t * `sweepStaleTranscripts`), and a cursor sitting legitimately at line 0 must\n199\t * not be mistaken for it.\n200\t */\n201\tasync function readCursor(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string): Promise<Cursor | null> {\n202\t  try {\n203\t    const raw = await readFile(cursorPath(repo, sessionId), \"utf8\");\n204\t    const data = JSON.parse(raw) as { lines?: number; size?: number };\n205\t    return {\n206\t      lines: typeof data.lines === \"number\" ? data.lines : 0,\n207\t      size: typeof data.size === \"number\" ? data.size : 0,\n208\t    };\n209\t  } catch {\n210\t    return null;\n211\t  }\n212\t}\n213\t\n214\t/**\n215\t * Record a cursor.\n216\t *\n217\t * Written to a temporary file and renamed, because a cursor now has two\n218\t * writers: the session's own hook, and any *other* session in the same\n219\t * project sweeping it (see `sweepStaleTranscripts`). `rename` is atomic\n220\t * within a directory, so a concurrent reader sees the old cursor or the new\n221\t * one, never a half-written file. 