{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"648\t/**\n649\t * Capture any *other* session in this project whose transcript has grown\n650\t * since it was last read.\n651\t *\n652\t * This exists because a session's own last lines are unreachable to it. The\n653\t * hook fires, capture reads to end-of-file, and Claude Code then writes more\n654\t * — the closing bookkeeping of the final turn, and crucially the session's\n655\t * last `file-history-snapshot`, which is the most complete one it will ever\n656\t * write. No further hook fires for that session, so those lines sat stranded\n657\t * behind a cursor nothing would ever advance again. Observed live: a cursor\n658\t * resting at line 40 of a 50-line transcript, with the only snapshot naming a\n659\t * real backup at line 49.\n660\t *\n661\t * The next session in the same project closes the gap. Staleness is decided\n662\t * by file size against the size recorded with the cursor, so the sweep stats\n663\t * each transcript rather than parsing it, and reads only the ones that grew.\n664\t *\n665\t * A transcript with *no* cursor is skipped, and that bound is the whole point\n666\t * of the pass. A missing cursor does not mean \"this session has a gap\", it\n667\t * means cledger never captured this session at all — it predates the install,\n668\t * or the user did not want it. Adopting those would turn a gap-closing sweep\n669\t * into a silent backfill of every conversation ever held in the repo, and\n670\t * would anchor each one to whatever HEAD happens to be checked out now rather\n671\t * than to the commit it was actually about. A session cledger already tracks\n672\t * is the only session it has any business finishing.\n673\t *\n674\t * Failures are swallowed per session: a sweep is a bonus pass over\n675\t * conversations the user is not currently having, and must never be the\n676\t * reason their live capture reports an error.\n677\t */\n678\tasync function sweepStaleTranscripts(\n679\t  transcriptPath: string,\n680\t  cwd: string,\n681\t  seen: Set<string>,\n682\t): Promise<void> {\n683\t  const repo = await findRepo(cwd);\n684\t  if (!repo) return;\n685\t  let entries: string[];\n686\t  try {\n687\t    entries = await readdir(dirname(transcriptPath));\n688\t  } catch {\n689\t    return;\n690\t  }\n691\t\n692\t  for (const name of entries) {\n693\t    if (!name.endsWith(\".jsonl\")) continue;\n694\t    const path = join(dirname(transcriptPath), name);\n695\t    if (seen.has(path)) continue;\n696\t    try {\n697\t      const cursor = await readCursor(repo, basename(name, \".jsonl\"));\n698\t      if (cursor === null) continue; // never captured — not this pass's business\n699\t      const info = await stat(path);\n700\t      if (info.size <= cursor.size) continue; // nothing new since the last read\n701\t      await captureClaudeTranscript(path, cwd, seen);\n702\t    } catch {\n703\t      continue;\n704\t    }\n705\t  }\n706\t}\n707\t\n708\texport async function runClaudeCodeHook(stdinJson: string): Promise<void> {\n709\t  try {\n710\t    const payload = JSON.parse(stdinJson) as ClaudeCodeHookPayload;\n711\t    const cwd = payload.cwd ?? process.cwd();\n712\t    if (!payload.transcript_path) return;\n713\t    const repo = await findRepo(cwd);\n714\t    if (!repo) return; // hooks must never break the user's session outside a repo\n715\t    const seen = new Set<string>();\n716\t    await captureClaudeTranscript(payload.transcript_path, cwd, seen);\n717\t    await sweepStaleTranscripts(payload.transcript_path, cwd, seen);\n718\t  } catch (err) {\n719\t    process.stderr.write(\n720\t      `cledger: claude-code hook error: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}\\n`,\n721\t    );\n722\t  }\n723\t}\n724\t\n725\t/**\n726\t * Capture one transcript file. Does not print, does not follow subagents —\n727\t * `captureClaudeTranscript` wraps this to do both.\n728\t */\n729\tasync function captureTranscriptFile(\n730\t  repo: RepoInfo,\n731\t  transcriptPath: string,\n732\t): Promise<CaptureResult> {\n733\t  const result: CaptureResult = { appended: 0, deduped: 0, unrecognized: {} };\n734\t  let raw: string;\n735\t  try {\n736\t    raw = await readFile(transcriptPath, \"utf8\");\n737\t  } catch {\n738\t    return result; // transcript not written yet\n739\t  }\n740\t  // Whether the writer had finished the last line when we read. A transcript\n741\t  // that does not end in a newline was caught mid-write, which is how the\n742\t  // final line comes to be torn — see `tornTail` below.\n743\t  const endsWithNewline = raw.endsWith(\"\\n\");\n744\t  const lines = raw.split(\"\\n\");\n745\t  if (lines.length > 0 && lines[lines.length - 1] === \"\") lines.pop();\n746\t\n747\t  const sessionId = basename(transcriptPath, \".jsonl\");","tool_use_id":"toolu_015HZn3qiyWdZbZbmgpcVs4V","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"0efe101ae3a794ff333e1c5b4122fdb71b3266fd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","seq":881},"id":"ev1-26e3ac18dbb9d013206f694493cfe1071f7c29d71122acb5a537dbd7171dfcdf","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T01:24:44.408Z","producer":{"session_id":"8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"648\t/**\n649\t * Capture any *other* session in this project whose transcript has grown\n650\t * since it was last read.\n651\t *\n652\t * This exists because a session's own last lines are unrea