 kind.\n\nGemini CLI (`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`) is the harder of\nthe two: the file is append-only but is a write-ahead log of mutations to one\nconversation document, not a transcript. Capture replays it with Gemini's own\nrecord precedence, but deliberately does not honour its removals — verified on\na live session, Gemini rewrote the document after a failed API call and\nsilently dropped the prompt the user had just typed. The ledger keeps the\nunion of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and\nrecords the `$rewindTo` itself as an `activity` naming what it withdrew, so a\nwithdrawn turn is legible as withdrawn rather than merely present. `$set`\npatches become `session_state`; `info`/`error`/`warning` notices become turns\nspoken by the system. Because nothing is removed, `seq` is assigned at first\nsighting over messages and mutations alike and never reused, so a rewind\ncannot renumber later turns. Sub-sessions under `<chats>/<parent id>/` are\ncaptured as sub-conversations.\n\nQwen Code (`~/.qwen/projects/<escaped-cwd>/chats/<id>.jsonl`) forked Gemini CLI\nbut not its store: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope,\nso the adapter is that adapter's twin — per-line conversion, line-index `seq`,\na torn-tail-safe cursor, the same catch-up sweep. Everything that is not a turn\narrives as a `system` line discriminated by `subtype`: `attribution_snapshot`\nbecomes `file_snapshot` (per-file content hashes are in the record itself, so\nnothing needs resolving against a local cache), the title/source/goal subtypes\nbecome `session_state`, `at_command` and the agent-launch prompts become\n`context_injection`, and everything else becomes `activity` rather than being\ndropped. A `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a sub-conversation.\n\nBoth CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion is\nshared in genai-parts.ts.\n\nAlso:\n- Extracts the cursor into adapters/common.ts and puts all five adapters on\n  it. 0.19.0 taught the claude-code cursor three things the others still did\n  not know — absent is not zero, `size` bounds the sweep, the write must be\n  atomic — and the fix for each was worth having everywhere rather than in one\n  of five copies.\n- Fixes the torn-trailing-line bug in codex, which 0.19.0 fixed for\n  claude-code only: the cursor advanced past a half-written line, so the\n  completed line was never captured. Uses the same narrow rule (unterminated\n  file *and* final line), because holding at any parse failure would stall a\n  session's capture forever on real corruption.\n- `cledger capture <gemini-cli|qwen-code> --all` backfills every session the\n  CLI scopes to this directory; the hook's own sweep is deliberately narrower\n  and only finishes sessions cledger already tracks.\n\nVerified end to end against live CLIs: `cledger install qwen-code` followed by\na real `qwen` run captures the session automatically — 6 turns, 2 file\nsnapshots and 5 activity records, with the machinery kinds correctly hidden\nfrom the default `log` view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg.txt","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"88f14ad9-bff3-470b-a8ce-3cedc048fae3","version":"2.1.223"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-06T01:44:21.078Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
